face-image: img/Fiume.jpg

= Occupation of Fiume

Gabriele D'Annunzio, a poet and officer of the <span style="color:#008C45">Regi</span><span style="color:#CFCFCF">o Eser</span><span style="color:#CD212A">cito</span>, along with his "legionaries", have seized control of the city of Fiume from <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#C8102E">Ent</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#000091">ente</span> occupying forces, declaring the "<span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">al</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ian</span> Regency of Carnaro" and demanding <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> annex the city.

D'Annunzio, accompanied by <span style="color:#2F2F2F">syndicalist</span> Alceste De Ambris, has surprisingly garnered the support of some of the left, most notably the <span style="color:#3D3D3D">national</span> <span style="color:#ED2855">syndicalist</span> *Italian Labour Union*, even as <span style="color:#C8102E">British</span> and <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#1E99C5">French</span> union organisations have called upon <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">al</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ian</span> workers to protest this perceived act of imperialism.

This has caused quite a stir internationally, and will certainly delay the resolution of our negotiations with <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#6A0080">Yugoslavia</span>.

- @support_fiume: Support D'Annunzio and his revolutionary march!
- @root: Do not release a comment.
- @condemn_fiume: Condemn D'Annunzio and his nationalist march! 

@condemn_fiume 
subtitle: D'Annunzio is popular among our veterans, who see him as regaining <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span>'s pride.
